## Authentication

Create a service key (Development → Keys → Service keys, as a super admin)
or a legacy private app in your HubSpot portal settings and copy its access
token. The provider reads the token from the `HUBSPOT_ACCESS_TOKEN`
environment variable:

```shell
export HUBSPOT_ACCESS_TOKEN="pat-..."
```

A token set explicitly in the provider configuration takes precedence over
the environment variable. Prefer the environment variable to keep credentials
out of your configuration files and state.

Every provider argument can be supplied through the environment:

| Provider argument | Environment variable | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `access_token` | `HUBSPOT_ACCESS_TOKEN` | (required, no default) |
| `base_url` | `HUBSPOT_BASE_URL` | `https://api.hubapi.com` |

See the [Authentication and scopes](guides/authentication.md) guide for the
service-key vs. private-app details, the per-resource scope matrix, and the
product-tier requirements.

### Terraform state and least privilege

The provider requests **only configuration scopes** — it never asks for CRM
record scopes and cannot read or modify your contacts, companies, or deals.
The `access_token` is a sensitive value; supplying it through
`HUBSPOT_ACCESS_TOKEN` keeps it out of your configuration and state entirely.
Treat state as sensitive regardless, and store it in a backend that supports
encryption.

